      "name": "The Golden Krone, Bistritz",
      "description": "The Golden Krone Hotel is thoroughly old-fashioned, all dark beams and lamplight, with a supper of robber steak and a bottle of Golden Mediasch laid on the table. It is the eve of St. George's Day, and the landlady crosses herself whenever the Count's name is spoken. Through the door to the east the diligence for Bukovina waits to start for the Borgo Pass.",
